{"assessments":[{"claimId":"claim-001","sourceExcerpt":"A hot spot is an airport movement-area location","sourceMeaning":"A hot spot is a location in an airport's movement area.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De definitie stemt overeen met de bewering.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-002","sourceExcerpt":"with a history or potential risk of collision","sourceMeaning":"The location has a history of collision, or a potential collision risk.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"Een voorgeschiedenis van een botsing wordt gedekt door “a history ... of collision”.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-003","sourceExcerpt":"or runway incursion","sourceMeaning":"The stated history or potential risk may also concern a runway incursion.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De bron noemt een runway incursion naast een botsing.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-004","sourceExcerpt":"or potential risk of collision or runway incursion","sourceMeaning":"A hot spot may have a potential risk of collision or runway incursion, without requiring a past incident.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De bron noemt potentieel risico als alternatief voor een voorgeschiedenis.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-005","sourceExcerpt":"The FAA standardized two meanings with three shapes beginning May 19, 2022.","sourceMeaning":"The FAA standardized two hot-spot meanings using three shapes, starting May 19, 2022.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De bron ondersteunt dat de FAA gestandaardiseerde vormen gebruikt om twee soorten te onderscheiden.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-006","sourceExcerpt":"beginning May 19, 2022","sourceMeaning":"The standardization began on May 19, 2022; the excerpt does not specify whether use continued without interruption afterward.","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE","material":true,"explanation":"De bron vermeldt de begindatum, maar bevestigt niet expliciet de voortduring die de claim als kwalificatie stelt.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-007","sourceExcerpt":"standardized two meanings","sourceMeaning":"The standard distinguishes two hot-spot meanings or types.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"Het aantal twee komt overeen met de bron.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-008","sourceExcerpt":"A circle or ellipse marks a ground movement hot spot","sourceMeaning":"A circle or ellipse represents a ground movement hot spot, one of the two types.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De bron noemt grondbewegingshotspots expliciet als een type.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-009","sourceExcerpt":"a cylinder marks a wrong surface hot spot","sourceMeaning":"A cylinder represents a wrong surface hot spot, one of the two types.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De bron noemt wrong surface hot spots expliciet als het andere type; de Nederlandse benaming duidt dit type aan.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-010","sourceExcerpt":"A hot spot is an airport movement-area location","sourceMeaning":"A hot spot is a location in an airport's movement area.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De herhaalde definitie komt overeen met de bron.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-011","sourceExcerpt":"with a history or potential risk of collision","sourceMeaning":"A hot spot may have a collision history or a potential collision risk; these are alternatives.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De contextsectie behoudt het onderscheid tussen voorgeschiedenis en potentieel risico.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-012","sourceExcerpt":"or runway incursion","sourceMeaning":"The stated history or potential risk may concern a runway incursion as well as a collision.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De bron noemt runway incursion als onderdeel van dezelfde definitie.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-013","sourceExcerpt":"beginning May 19, 2022","sourceMeaning":"The FAA standardization began on May 19, 2022.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De datum en de start van de standaard komen overeen met de bron.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-014","sourceExcerpt":"A circle or ellipse marks a ground movement hot spot","sourceMeaning":"A circle or ellipse represents a ground movement hot spot; the shapes are alternatives.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De kaartvormen en het aangeduide type komen overeen.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-015","sourceExcerpt":"a cylinder marks a wrong surface hot spot","sourceMeaning":"A cylinder represents a wrong surface hot spot.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De kaartvorm en het aangeduide type komen overeen.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-016","sourceExcerpt":"The stated purpose is to prevent confusion about the meaning or depiction of hot spots.","sourceMeaning":"The shapes distinguish the two hot-spot meanings.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De bron vermeldt twee betekenissen en bijbehorende vormen; de narrative beschrijft dat deze vormen de betekenissen onderscheiden.","correction":null},{"claimId":"claim-017","sourceExcerpt":"The stated purpose is to prevent confusion about the meaning or depiction of hot spots.","sourceMeaning":"Preventing confusion about hot-spot meaning or depiction is the stated purpose, not a proven outcome.","verdict":"SUPPORTED","material":false,"explanation":"De narrative presenteert dit als doel en niet als bewezen resultaat.","correction":null}],"coverageQuestions":[]}

